  "id": "residual-error",
  "term": "residual error",
  "definition": "Residual error is the refractive error that remains after a toric intraocular lens is implanted, especially when the lens is not perfectly aligned. In this source, it refers to the remaining astigmatic or related optical error produced by lens rotation, axial shift, or both.",
